s Checklist\\n\\n- [ ] Every code producer updated or verified compatible \u2014 new agents (`skill-auditor`, `skill-content-updater`) created with correct trigger keywords; `skill-sync` skill created\\n- [ ] Every code consumer migrated or verified compatible \u2014 all 6 skills/agents routing to removed agent updated to new targets; content-optimization concern must have an explicit routing target before consumer updates can complete\\n- [ ] Every affected test updated or new coverage added \u2014 `test_auto_sync_manifests.py` verified compatible with new agent count; new tests for `skill-sync` orchestration added\\n- [ ] Every stale document updated \u2014 12 documentation files updated including CLAUDE.md, README, workflow diagrams, phase-skill-mapping, agent-examples\\n- [ ] Every affected config or CI path updated and validated \u2014 plugin.json version bump verified; auto_sync_manifests.py behavior verified for agent rename/add scenario\\n- [ ] Every affected agent or skill instruction updated \u2014 all 8 agent-instruction files across plugin-creator and the-rewrite-room updated to route to replacement agents\\n- [ ] Replacement or migration coverage gaps resolved \u2014 content-optimization concern must be explicitly assigned to a named replacement agent before any removal of the original file\\n- [ ] Hidden transitive dependencies checked \u2014 the-rewrite-room plugin dependency on plugin-creator:contextual-ai-documentation-optimizer is a cross-plugin runtime dependency; plugin versioning must account for this; users with plugin-creator installed but not updated will break\\n</div>\\n\\n## Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAlignment assessment: **DIVERGENT**\\n\\n### Divergences\\n\\n| Area | Expected (Design Intent) | Actual (Implementation) | Severity | File |\\n|------|--------------------------|-------------------------|----------|------|\\n| New `/skill-sync` skill | Orchestration skill with parallel read agents (completeness auditor, upstream drift researcher, structure validator), synthesis step, schema-aware write agent | Skill does not exist | missing | plugins/plugin-creator/skills/ |\\n| New `skill-auditor` agent | Agent absorbing quality audit concern from split | Agent does not exist | missing | plugins/plugin-creator/agents/ |\\n| New `skill-content-updater` agent | Agent absorbing upstream sync concern from split, primary purpose of this item | Agent does not exist | missing | plugins/plugin-creator/agents/ |\\n| `contextual-ai-documentation-optimizer` split | Description should accurately name all 3 bundled concerns; agent should be split into focused replacements | Agent remains bundled; description names only 1 concern (optimization) while skills array proves 3 bundled concerns | functional | plugins/plugin-creator/agents/contextual-ai-documentation-optimizer.md:3 |\\n| `/optimize-claude-md` Phase 3 routing | Should route to whichever new agent absorbs content-optimization concern | Routes to `@contextual-ai-documentation-optimizer` (still bundled, unchanged) | functional | plugins/plugin-creator/skills/optimize-claude-md/SKILL.md:52,106-110 |\\n\\n### Summary\\n\\n5 divergences: 0 functional (routing still references unchanged agent), 2 functional (bundled agent not split; description does not match actual concerns), 3 missing (new skill and two new agents do not exist).\\n\\n**Context**: This is a **new feature item** (#1899). The design intent describes creating entirely new components (`/skill-sync` skill, `skill-auditor` agent, `skill-content-updater` agent) and refactoring the existing `contextual-ai-documentation-optimizer` agent. Since the item is open with status \\\"open\\\" and no implementation has been started, the divergence is **expected and architectural** \u2014 the feature has not yet been built. This is not a regression or a deviation from specification; it is an unfulfilled design specification waiting for implementation work.\\n\\nThe item's design intent is clear, complete, and well-grounded in the RT-ICA analysis and Impact Radius sections. Once implementation begins, these divergences should move from MISSING/DIVERGENT to ALIGNED.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **plugin-creator: no single-invocation skill update workflow; manual content updates produce sk007 violations and incorrect agent selection** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 2026-04-23 drift audit of plugin-creator skills against upstream documentation\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-23\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n\\n<!-- artifact-gist:2efc27bc1c4363d4b81adaac2e33e3b4 -->\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\nN/A \u2014 feature request. No reproduction steps needed. The absence of the workflow is itself the observable condition.\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n8/10 \u2014 The missing workflow produces two structurally guaranteed failure modes with no current workaround: (1) the SK007 pre-commit gate fires after content is written, so any drift-audit content addition that pushes a skill over the 8800-token limit blocks the commit and forces a remediation pass before pushing can proceed; (2) `contextual-ai-documentation-optimizer` names only one of its three bundled concerns, so orchestrators systematically mis-route audit and upstream-sync work to general-purpose agents. Both failures were demonstrated on 2026-04-23 during a real drift audit. The blast radius is 104 references across three plugins with cross-plugin runtime dispatch paths that break immediately on any migration. Ranked P1 rather than P0 because the current system still functions (drift audits can be completed with extra manual passes), but the cost multiplier grows with every additional skill that goes above the token threshold.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: every developer running a drift audit on plugin-creator skills; the missing workflow forces manual multi-step orchestration with no established routing or token-budget guardrail\\n- Bottleneck: the agent description mismatch for `contextual-ai-documentation-optimizer` causes systematic mis-routing \u2014 audit and upstream-sync tasks land on general-purpose agents instead of the purpose-built agent, with no correction point in the pipeline\\n- Cross-plugin dispatch risk: `the-rewrite-room` plugin dispatches live tasks to `contextual-ai-documentation-optimizer` across a plugin boundary (7 files including 2 runtime agents and a workflow file); any rename without a coordinated migration breaks `the-rewrite-room` immediately at task execution time\\n- Commit-time cost: SK007 violations surface at `git commit`, after content is written; each violation requires a second remediation agent pass before the branch can be pushed, multiplying the work for every oversized content addition\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- A drifted skill can be brought to compliance and committed in a single invocation \u2014 no manual multi-step orchestration required\\n- SK007 violations are prevented before content is written, eliminating post-write remediation passes and unblocking commit queues\\n- Each plugin-creator agent's description accurately enumerates the concerns it handles, making the correct agent discoverable for audit-only, upstream-sync, and content-optimization tasks without manual routing\\n- `the-rewrite-room` and all other cross-plugin consumers resolve to valid, appropriately-scoped agents instead of a removed or misdescribed bundled agent\\n- `populate-agent-descriptions.mjs` continues to execute without referencing a non-existent agent filename\\n- New tests cover the `skill-sync` orchestration path and the updated agent-count arithmetic in `test_auto_sync_manifests.py`\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen a developer invokes the skill-sync workflow on a skill whose cited upstream documentation has changed, the system first reads the existing skill file and surfaces which sections consume the most tokens, so the write step operates within a known budget before any file is modified. The system then: (a) determines whether the proposed content would exceed the SK007 token limit before writing anything, refusing to write if it would; (b) applies the upstream changes through an agent whose description explicitly names upstream-sync as a handled concern; (c) runs a post-write skilllint pass to verify SK007 compliance; (d) produces a committed, linted-passing file without requiring a separate remediation pass.\\n\\nWhen a developer selects an agent for a quality-audit task, they can identify the appropriate agent by reading that agent's description field alone \u2014 no bundled, unnamed concerns are present.\\n\\nWhen any consumer in `plugin-creator`, `the-rewrite-room`, or `development-harness` references an agent by name, that name resolves to an existing agent file that handles the concern the consumer intends.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. Before any file is written, the skill-sync workflow outputs a section-level token breakdown for the existing skill file, identifying which sections consume the most tokens \u2014 observable as structured output naming each section and its token count prior to the write step.\\n2. A skill file that would exceed the SK007 limit (8800 tokens) after a content addition is not written by the skill-sync workflow \u2014 the write is refused before any file is modified, not at commit time.\\n3. A skill file that is within the SK007 limit after a content addition is written, linted, and committed without manual intervention via a single workflow invocation.\\n4. `uvx skilllint@latest check plugins/plugin-creator/` exits 0 with no SK007 errors after the skill-sync workflow completes (post-write verification pass, not only pre-write estimation).\\n5. Every agent in `plugins/plugin-creator/agents/` has a description field that explicitly names each concern its loaded skills address \u2014 no concern is bundled but absent from the description.\\n6. Running `grep -r 'contextual-ai-documentation-optimizer' plugins/` returns zero results across all runtime agent files, workflow files, CLAUDE.md files, and skill instruction files in `plugin-creator`, `the-rewrite-room`, and `development-harness`.\\n7. `node plugins/plugin-creator/skills/agent-capability-analyzer/scripts/populate-agent-descriptions.mjs` executes without error (all referenced agent filenames exist on disk).\\n8. `uv run pytest plugins/plugin-creator/tests/test_auto_sync_manifests.py` passes with the new agent count in place.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Skill | /plugin-creator:audit-skill-completeness \u2014 standalone quality-audit skill, VERIFIED present |\\n| Skill | /plugin-creator:write-frontmatter-description \u2014 standalone frontmatter description skill, VERIFIED present |\\n| Skill | /plugin-creator:prompt-optimization \u2014 content-optimization skill, bundled in current agent |\\n| Agent | plugin-creator:assessor \u2014 existing parallel-agent orchestration pattern reference |\\n| Agent | plugin-creator:refactor-executor \u2014 existing runtime dispatch pattern reference |\\n| Agent | plugin-creator:refactor-planner \u2014 existing plan-generation pattern reference |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/plugin-creator/agents/contextual-ai-documentation-optimizer.md` \u2014 source agent being split |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/agent-capability-analyzer/scripts/populate-agent-descriptions.mjs` \u2014 JS registry requiring code change at line 392 |\\n\\n### Files\\n\\nHigh-risk files requiring change (from Impact Radius / Systems Inventory):\\n\\n**New files to create**\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/agents/skill-auditor.md` \u2014 new agent absorbing quality-audit concern\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/agents/skill-content-updater.md` \u2014 new agent absorbing upstream-sync concern\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-sync/SKILL.md` \u2014 new single-invocation workflow skill\\n\\n**Agent to rename/rework**\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/agents/contextual-ai-documentation-optimizer.md` \u2192 `ai-doc-optimizer.md` (content-optimization scope only, description updated to match)\\n\\n**Runtime agent instructions (break immediately on removal)**\\n- `plugins/the-rewrite-room/agents/rewrite-room-optimizer.md` \u2014 cross-plugin dispatch to removed agent\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/agents/refactor-executor.md` \u2014 live DOC_IMPROVE dispatch\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/agents/refactor-planner.md` \u2014 plan output names removed agent\\n- `plugins/the-rewrite-room/the-rewrite-room/workflows/optimize.md` \u2014 9 Mermaid branches\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/plugin-lifecycle/SKILL.md` \u2014 inline delegation instruction\\n\\n**Hard-coded registry (code break, not doc drift)**\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/agent-capability-analyzer/scripts/populate-agent-descriptions.mjs:392`\\n\\n**Consumer skills (routing breaks)**\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/optimize-claude-md/SKILL.md`\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/implement-refactor/SKILL.md`\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/assessor/SKILL.md`\\n\\n**AI-facing documentation (drives runtime routing)**\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/CLAUDE.md` (lines 96, 220, 225-226, 399-410, 484, 492)\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/plugin-creator/references/workflow-diagram.md` (8 locations)\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/plugin-lifecycle/references/phase-skill-mapping.md`\\n\\n**Tests**\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/tests/test_auto_sync_manifests.py`\\n\\n**Configuration**\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/.claude-plugin/plugin.json` (auto-bumped on agent CRUD)\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: content-optimization concern split-target decision \u2014 RESOLVED by orchestrator (rename to `ai-doc-optimizer`, content-optimization scope only); no remaining MISSING conditions\\n- Depends on: `auto_sync_manifests.py` version-bump behavior must handle rename (delete + add) without triggering an unintended MAJOR version bump before the MINOR adds land; verify test compatibility before agent file is deleted\\n- Blocks: any downstream consumer migration in `the-rewrite-room` and `development-harness` \u2014 those 7+ files cannot be updated to route to the new agents until the new agent files exist on disk\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nHigh \u2014 involves creating a new skill directory (`skill-sync`), creating 2 new agent files, renaming/reworking 1 existing agent, updating 8 runtime agent-instruction files across 2 plugins (immediate breakage risk), patching 1 JavaScript registry file (code change, not doc update), updating 12+ documentation files, and verifying/updating 3 test files. Cross-plugin scope (plugin-creator, the-rewrite-room, development-harness) and the hard-coded JS registry entry elevate risk and coordination cost above a typical single-plugin refactor.\\n\\n### Concerns\\n\\n- [x] SEMVER: plugin-creator Wave A landed at 13.1.0 (MINOR) instead of 14.0.0 (MAJOR). Root cause: plugin.json pre-staged before hook ran; _version_already_bumped guard exited early. Functional impact nil. Corrective action: bump to 14.0.0. (reported by T4.2) \u2192 backlog item creation deferred\\n- [ ] CLAUDE.md agents table: Model column shows sonnet for skill-auditor and skill-content-updater, but both use model: inherit. (reported by qg-t0 T0, Q1)\\n- [ ] ai-doc-optimizer.md has no tools: field; sibling agents skill-auditor and skill-content-updater both declare explicit tools. (reported by qg-t0 T0, Q2)\\n- [ ] skill-sync/SKILL.md Stage 2: agents 2 and 3 lack Agent() dispatch syntax; only agent 1 is fully specified. (reported by qg-t0 T0, Q3)\\n- [ ] refactor-executor.md and refactor-planner.md missing STATUS: DONE terminal block per agent-output-contracts.md (pre-existing, not a regression). (reported by qg-t0 T0, Q5)\\n\\n### Design Intent Alignment\\n\\nAlignment assessment: DIVERGENT (expected \u2014 feature not yet implemented)\\n\\n| Design intent | Current state | Verdict |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `/skill-sync` orchestration skill exists | Not present in plugins/plugin-creator/skills/ | DIVERGENT |\\n| `skill-auditor` agent exists | Not present in plugins/plugin-creator/agents/ | DIVERGENT |\\n| `skill-content-updater` agent exists | Not present in plugins/plugin-creator/agents/ | DIVERGENT |\\n| `ai-doc-optimizer` agent (renamed from contextual-ai-documentation-optimizer) exists | Original agent present, not yet renamed | DIVERGENT |\\n| 104 references updated to route to correct split agent | References updated with routing notes but still name the original agent | DIVERGENT |\\n\\nAll divergences are the planned work. No unintended implementation exists that conflicts with the design intent. Once implemented, all items should resolve to ALIGNED.\\n\\n### Divergences\\n\\n| Area | Expected (Design Intent) | Actual (Implementation) | Severity | File |\\n|------|--------------------------|-------------------------|----------|------|\\n| New `/skill-sync` skill | Orchestration skill with parallel read agents (completeness auditor, upstream drift researcher, structure validator), synthesis step, schema-aware write agent | Skill does not exist | missing | plugins/plugin-creator/skills/ |\\n| New `skill-auditor` agent | Agent absorbing quality audit concern from split | Agent does not exist | missing | plugins/plugin-creator/agents/ |\\n| New `skill-content-updater` agent | Agent absorbing upstream sync concern from split, primary purpose of this item | Agent does not exist | missing | plugins/plugin-creator/agents/ |\\n| `contextual-ai-documentation-optimizer` split | Description should accurately name all 3 bundled concerns; agent should be split into focused replacements | Agent remains bundled; description names only 1 concern (optimization) while skills array proves 3 bundled concerns | functional | plugins/plugin-creator/agents/contextual-ai-documentation-optimizer.md:3 |\\n| `/optimize-claude-md` Phase 3 routing | Should route to whichever new agent absorbs content-optimization concern | Routes to `@contextual-ai-documentation-optimizer` (still bundled, unchanged) | functional | plugins/plugin-creator/skills/optimize-claude-md/SKILL.md:52,106-110 |\\n| Anti-Goal #3 (design decision resolved 2026-05-20) | Pre-write token profiling surfaces budget constraints before write; post-write skilllint verifies compliance \u2014 two-layer approach | Prior stance was post-write remediation loop only; design decision resolved: pre-write token distribution analyzer is now part of the workflow | design-note | N/A \u2014 resolved decision, no implementation gap |\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Type**: missing-guardrail\\n**Rationale**: The system allowed two bad outcomes that pre-write validation gates should have prevented: (1) content was written to `skill-creator/SKILL.md` (9161 tokens) and committed before any check confirmed it would pass SK007 (limit 8800); the pre-commit hook fires post-write, making it a late gate that produces remediation work rather than prevention. (2) `contextual-ai-documentation-optimizer` lacks an accurate description of its three bundled concerns, causing agents to skip it during routing \u2014 a discoverable-at-design-time naming failure with no correction mechanism. No prior issues in the backlog match these two failure modes (searched: SK007, token limit, skill update workflow, contextual-ai-documentation-optimizer). The root gap is structural: the plugin-creator update path has no pre-write budget validation and no agent discoverability contract, so both failures were architecturally guaranteed.\\n**Analysis Method**: 5-whys\\n**Scenario Target**: Developer runs drift audit \u2192 delegates content additions to general-purpose agent \u2192 agent writes oversized SKILL.md \u2192 pre-commit hook blocks commit \u2192 developer must do remediation pass \u2192 pushing delayed. With guardrails: skill-sync workflow checks token budget before write and routes through a description-accurate agent, eliminating both the block and the remediation pass.\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe plugin-creator plugin has no orchestrated single-invocation workflow for updating skill files after upstream documentation changes.\\n\\n**What is missing**: No workflow exists that checks token budget before writing, fetches upstream sources cited in a skill, and applies changes through a schema-aware agent. The `contextual-ai-documentation-optimizer` agent bundles three distinct concerns (quality auditing, content optimization, frontmatter description writing) under a description that names only one (\\\"optimize\\\"), making it undiscoverable when the task is updating skill content against upstream sources.\\n\\n**Where observed**: During the 2026-04-23 drift audit of plugin-creator skills against 9 upstream documentation URLs (`skills.md`, `plugins-reference.md`, `hooks.md`, `agent-teams.md`, `sub-agents.md`, `headless.md`, `scheduled-tasks.md`, `output-styles.md`, `agentskills.io/specification`). Content additions were delegated to general-purpose agents. This produced an SK007 token limit violation on `skill-creator/SKILL.md` (9161 tokens, limit 8800) that blocked the git commit pre-commit hook after the content was already written.\\n\\n**Impact**:\\n- Skill updates require multi-step manual agent orchestration with no established routing\\n- Agent selection fails because `contextual-ai-documentation-optimizer`'s description does not surface it for content-update tasks\\n- SK007 violations are discovered at commit time, after content is written, requiring a second remediation pass that blocks pushing\\n\\n**User-provided context** (design ideas \u2014 not requirements):\\nA `/simplify`-style skill with three parallel read agents (completeness auditor, upstream drift researcher, structure validator), an orchestrator synthesis step applying precedence rules, and a schema-aware write agent that executes only the produced change plan. Also split `contextual-ai-documentation-optimizer` into focused agents with descriptions that accurately name each concern.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n| Claim | Verdict | Evidence Quality |\\n|-------|---------|-----------------|\\n| 1. contextual-ai-documentation-optimizer description names only one concern | VERIFIED | Strong \u2014 agent file directly examined |\\n| 2. SK007 violation at 9,161 tokens blocked commit pre-commit hook | INCONCLUSIVE | Current state contradicts claim; past state unverifiable |\\n| 3. No single-invocation skill update workflow exists | VERIFIED | Strong \u2014 comprehensive directory search |\\n| 4. /simplify uses 3 parallel review agents | INCONCLUSIVE | Not documented in official Claude Code docs |\\n| 5. Both skills exist as standalone | VERIFIED | Strong \u2014 files directly examined and confirmed user-invocable |\\n</div>\\n\\n## Recommendations\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Claim 1 (VERIFIED)**: Use this as design justification for splitting contextual-ai-documentation-optimizer\\n- **Claim 2 (INCONCLUSIVE)**: Document current token count in issue if re-running the drift audit; verify skilllint token measurement methodology\\n- **Claim 3 (VERIFIED)**: Confirms the core problem statement of the issue\\n- **Claim 4 (INCONCLUSIVE)**: If /simplify architecture is intended as the reference pattern, cite it from internal anthropics documentation or verify its current implementation\\n- **Claim 5 (VERIFIED)**: Confirmed prerequisite skills exist for the proposed solution\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"31b32dcd11cc40f92f26fb1be26e9e28862aec6c746285738703f5d2ec7e2674\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPvckHg\"}"}